    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Handling Missing Data and Patterns"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Sometimes, you need to search using incomplete or partial data. For example, you need to find employees who are missing last_name and whose first_name ends in 'e'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Filter for Missing Data:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1-- Find employees with missing last names\n2\n3SELECT *\n4FROM Employees\n5WHERE last_name IS NULL;"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Unlike known values, you cannot use comparison operators when working with NULL. Instead, use IS NULL or IS NOT NULL."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. Add a pattern match for first_name:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1-- Find employees with specific name patterns\n2\n3SELECT *\n4FROM Employees\n5WHERE last_name IS NULL\n6AND first_name LIKE '%e';"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The LIKE clause, combined with wildcards (% for zero or more characters, _ for a single character), allows you to search for patterns in text."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Idea Emoji",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You can apply these filtering techniques to other tables and scenarios whenever necessary."
    },
